{"change_summary":"Implemented the remaining round-10 amendments for per-tick budget tracking. In `nitrogen_cycle.rs`, decomposer remineralization now uses a debug-assert-backed residual clamp so tiny floating-point negatives still clamp to zero but larger logic errors trip in debug builds instead of being silently swallowed. In `budget_tracking.rs`, added a dedicated `SiphonDetritus` regression that runs a tracked tick, verifies the expected nitrogen/carbon export from particulate and fine detritus, and confirms the `action:siphon_detritus` ledger entry records explicit outflow rather than unexplained loss. In the carbonate/source-water path, `chemistry.rs` now tracks when the solver had to fall back to the non-finite neutral pH path and `validate_source_water_carbonate_profile()` rejects that case explicitly; `SourceWaterProfile::validate()` and `tank_data` preset validation were updated to surface that failure, with new regression coverage in both crates.","outstanding_risks":["The canonical helper coverage guard for element-bearing state is still convention-based rather than reflective; future explicit N/C pools with non-standard names will require updating the discovery rules and tests together.","Complex multi-process stages such as `system:nitrogen_cycle` still rely on snapshot-derived gross component budgets, so same-component turnover inside a single stage can remain collapsed until those systems emit fully explicit source/sink deltas.","The new carbonate validation only special-cases the known non-finite neutral fallback path. If future solver changes introduce a different internal failure mode, the validation helper will need to be extended in lockstep.","The worktree also contains unrelated pre-existing changes outside this task in `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs`, `crates/tank_core/src/types/water.rs`, `crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs`, plus untracked `.ralph-burning/` content."],"steps":[{"description":"Audited the pending amendments against the current nitrogen-cycle clamps, `SiphonDetritus` budget recording, and source-water carbonate validation path to confirm the remaining gaps on HEAD.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Patched `tank_core` so decomposer post-growth residuals assert past a small rounding tolerance in debug builds, and added explicit carbonate-validation status plumbing so non-finite neutral fallback solves are rejected for source-water validation.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Added regression coverage for explicit `SiphonDetritus` N/C exports plus new runtime and preset tests that reject overflowed carbonate source-water profiles instead of accepting the neutral fallback.","order":3,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Ran formatting, focused regression suites, full `tank_core` validation, and clippy across the touched crates to confirm the amendments pass cleanly.","order":4,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all -- --check` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test budget_tracking --test chemistry --test water_change_mass_balance` passed (49 tests total, including the new `SiphonDetritus` export regression and non-finite carbonate fallback rejection tests).","`cargo test -p tank_data` passed (5 tests, including the new source-water preset non-finite fallback rejection regression).","`cargo test -p tank_core` passed across the full `tank_core` suite (188 tests across 23 test binaries).","`cargo clippy -p tank_core -p tank_data -- -D warnings` passed."]}